From: Try Omarchy contributors
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: keep App Nap off while the VM runs

Applies after the other Try Omarchy Cocoa patches.

macOS naps an app none of whose windows can be seen: the screen locked, the
VM's full screen on another Space, the window minimized or covered. A napped
QEMU runs every thread, the vCPUs too, at background priority and the guest
crawls. OmacVM (MIT) measured 2-20 % of normal guest speed on an M4 Max with
the screen locked and four busy vCPUs, and fixed it the same way. Hold an
NSProcessInfo activity (NSActivityUserInitiatedAllowingIdleSystemSleep) from
the start of the run loop: the VM keeps working out of sight, as UTM's and
Parallels' VM processes do, and an idle Mac can still sleep. The macOS helper
pauses the VM for Mac sleep on its own. TRYOMARCHY_APP_NAP=1 leaves the
activity out, for measurements. QEMU's log says which applies.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -2469,8 +2469,36 @@ static void cocoa_clipboard_request(QemuClipboardInfo *info,
     }
 }
 
+/*
+ * macOS naps an app none of whose windows can be seen (the screen locked, the
+ * VM's full screen on another Space, the window minimized or covered). Every
+ * QEMU thread, the vCPUs too, then runs at background priority, and the guest
+ * slows to a fraction of its speed. Hold an activity for the whole run so the
+ * VM keeps working while nobody looks at it; idle system sleep stays allowed,
+ * and the app pauses the VM itself for Mac sleep. TRYOMARCHY_APP_NAP=1 lets
+ * macOS nap it, for measurements.
+ */
+static void cocoa_hold_no_app_nap_activity(void)
+{
+    static id activity;
+    const char *allow = getenv("TRYOMARCHY_APP_NAP");
+
+    if (activity) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (allow && strcmp(allow, "1") == 0) {
+        info_report("Try Omarchy: App Nap allowed (TRYOMARCHY_APP_NAP=1)");
+        return;
+    }
+    activity = [[[NSProcessInfo processInfo]
+        beginActivityWithOptions:NSActivityUserInitiatedAllowingIdleSystemSleep
+                          reason:@"Omarchy is running"] retain];
+    info_report("Try Omarchy: App Nap off while the VM runs");
+}
+
 static int cocoa_main(void)
 {
+    cocoa_hold_no_app_nap_activity();
     COCOA_DEBUG("Main thread: entering OSX run loop\n");
     [NSApp run];
     COCOA_DEBUG("Main thread: left OSX run loop, which should never happen\n");
